Epigenetic, once again, meaning that one level has to be fulfilled, or at least partly fulfilled, before we can go to the next level.

51
00:07:06,980 --> 00:07:15,080
And the three levels are dependent self-esteem, independent self-esteem, and unconditional self-esteem.

52
00:07:15,580 --> 00:07:19,840
Dependent self-esteem, the two components of it.

53
00:07:19,960 --> 00:07:34,420
First of all, a person with high dependence needs the accolades of others constantly, chooses whether it's a career path or what to do this afternoon, based on how much approval that will gain him or her.

54
00:07:34,420 --> 00:07:42,500
A person with dependent self-esteem, when it comes to competence, always compares him or herself to others.

55
00:07:43,460 --> 00:07:46,980
Am I better or am I worse? Superior or inferior?

56
00:07:49,670 --> 00:07:53,070
Independent self-esteem is self-esteem that's contingent on the self.

57
00:07:53,950 --> 00:08:05,490
In terms of how I evaluate myself, it's my internal voice that's speaking. In terms of how my levels of competence are determined, it depends on how much I've improved,

58
