how much better I've got, how much I feel that I've fulfilled my potential.

59
00:08:10,090 --> 00:08:14,530
That's independent self-esteem, not contingent on what other people say or think.

60
00:08:16,450 --> 00:08:20,830
Unconditional self-esteem is the highest level.

61
00:08:21,310 --> 00:08:24,610
The level that Maslow would talk about is self-actualization,

62
00:08:25,210 --> 00:08:33,470
what David Schnark talks about as differentiated, or at the level of being known rather than desiring to be validated.

63
00:08:35,790 --> 00:08:46,350
Unconditional self-esteem is when our self-esteem is high enough, we feel good enough about ourselves, not to be concerned with evaluation of others or even with self-evaluation.

64
00:08:48,720 --> 00:08:53,280
In terms of comparison, we don't compare. We're interdependent, connected to others.

